Database migrations must be backward compatible to support rolling deployments. Strategies: 1) Expand-contract pattern - add new, migrate data, update code, remove old, 2) Feature flags around new schema, 3) Migrations before deployment, rollback scripts prepared. Flyway/Liquibase integration:
spring.flyway.enabled=true
spring.flyway.locations=classpath:db/migration

Migration naming: V001__create_users.sql, V002__add_email_to_users.sql. Pipeline:
stage('Database Migration') {
  steps {
    sh 'java -jar app.jar --spring.flyway.migrate-only=true'
    // Application start handles migration
  }
}
stage('Deploy Application') {
  steps {
    sh 'kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml'
  }
}

Example breaking change - rename column: 1) V010: Add new_column, 2) V011: Dual write to both columns, 3) Deploy app version writing to both, 4) V012: Backfill data, 5) Deploy app version reading from new_column, 6) V013: Drop old_column. Each step independently deployable. Rollback: Flyway doesn't support down migrations, prepare rollback scripts manually if needed or use Liquibase rollback tags.

Feature flags control feature availability at runtime without redeployment. Enables deploying incomplete features disabled, testing in production with subset of users, instant rollback. Types: 1) Release flags - long-lived, control feature rollout, 2) Experiment flags - A/B testing, 3) Ops flags - circuit breakers, kill switches, 4) Permission flags - role-based features. Implementation:
@Configuration
public class FeatureFlags {
  @Value("${features.new-payment-flow}")
  private boolean newPaymentFlow;

  public boolean isNewPaymentFlowEnabled(User user) {
    if (!newPaymentFlow) return false;
    // Gradual rollout
    return user.getId() % 100 < 10; // 10% of users
  }
}

@Service
public class PaymentService {
  @Autowired FeatureFlags flags;

  public void processPayment(Order order, User user) {
    if (flags.isNewPaymentFlowEnabled(user)) {
      newPaymentProcessor.process(order);
    } else {
      legacyPaymentProcessor.process(order);
    }
  }
}

Tools: LaunchDarkly, Unleash, Split.io, or simple config server. Merge incomplete feature to main behind disabled flag, continue development, enable gradually when ready. Instant rollback: disable flag via config, no redeployment.

End-to-end pipeline from commit to production:
pipeline {
  agent any
  environment {
    DOCKER_REGISTRY = 'company.registry.io'
    APP_NAME = 'payment-service'
    K8S_NAMESPACE = 'production'
  }
  stages {
    stage('Checkout') {
      steps {
        checkout scm
        script {
          GIT_COMMIT_SHORT = sh(returnStdout: true, script: 'git rev-parse --short HEAD').trim()
          IMAGE_TAG = "${GIT_COMMIT_SHORT}"
        }
      }
    }
    stage('Build') {
      steps {
        sh 'mvn clean package -DskipTests'
      }
    }
    stage('Unit Tests') {
      steps {
        sh 'mvn test'
        junit 'target/surefire-reports/**/*.xml'
      }
    }
    stage('Code Quality') {
      steps {
        sh 'mvn sonar:sonar -Dsonar.host.url=http://sonarqube:9000'
      }
    }
    stage('Build Docker Image') {
      steps {
        sh "docker build -t ${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG} ."
        sh "docker tag ${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG} ${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:latest"
      }
    }
    stage('Security Scan') {
      steps {
        sh "trivy image ${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG}"
      }
    }
    stage('Push Image') {
      steps {
        sh "docker push ${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG}"
        sh "docker push ${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:latest"
      }
    }
    stage('Deploy to Dev') {
      steps {
        sh "kubectl set image deployment/${APP_NAME} ${APP_NAME}=${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG} -n dev"
        sh "kubectl rollout status deployment/${APP_NAME} -n dev --timeout=5m"
      }
    }
    stage('Integration Tests') {
      steps {
        sh './run-integration-tests.sh dev'
      }
    }
    stage('Deploy to Staging') {
      steps {
        sh "kubectl set image deployment/${APP_NAME} ${APP_NAME}=${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG} -n staging"
        sh "kubectl rollout status deployment/${APP_NAME} -n staging --timeout=5m"
      }
    }
    stage('Smoke Tests') {
      steps {
        sh './run-smoke-tests.sh staging'
      }
    }
    stage('Production Approval') {
      when { branch 'main' }
      steps {
        input message: 'Deploy to Production?', ok: 'Deploy'
      }
    }
    stage('Deploy to Production') {
      when { branch 'main' }
      steps {
        sh "kubectl set image deployment/${APP_NAME} ${APP_NAME}=${DOCKER_REGISTRY}/${APP_NAME}:${IMAGE_TAG} -n production"
        sh "kubectl rollout status deployment/${APP_NAME} -n production --timeout=10m"
      }
    }
    stage('Verify Production') {
      steps {
        sh './verify-production.sh'
        sh 'curl https://payment-service.prod/actuator/health'
      }
    }
  }
  post {
    success {
      slackSend(channel: '#deployments', message: "${APP_NAME} ${IMAGE_TAG} deployed successfully")
    }
    failure {
      slackSend(channel: '#deployments', message: "${APP_NAME} ${IMAGE_TAG} deployment failed", color: 'danger')
    }
  }
}

Complete flow takes ~20 minutes commit-to-prod with quality gates at each stage.

Approval gates pause pipeline for manual validation or external checks. Types: 1) Manual approval - requires human decision, 2) Automated gates - conditions must pass (test coverage, security scan, performance benchmarks), 3) Time-based gates - deploy only during business hours. Jenkins manual approval:
stage('Production Approval') {
  steps {
    script {
      def userInput = input(
        message: 'Deploy to Production?',
        parameters: [
          booleanParam(name: 'DEPLOY', defaultValue: false, description: 'Check to deploy'),
          text(name: 'NOTES', defaultValue: '', description: 'Deployment notes')
        ],
        submitterParameter: 'APPROVER'
      )
      echo "Approved by: ${userInput.APPROVER}"
      echo "Notes: ${userInput.NOTES}"
    }
  }
}

Automated quality gate:
stage('Quality Gate') {
  steps {
    script {
      def coverage = sh(returnStdout: true, script: 'mvn jacoco:report | grep "Total.*[0-9]*%"').trim()
      if (coverage.toInteger() < 80) {
        error('Code coverage below 80%, deployment blocked')
      }

      def sonarStatus = sh(returnStdout: true, script: 'curl sonarqube-api/quality-gate').trim()
      if (sonarStatus != 'OK') {
        error('SonarQube quality gate failed')
      }
    }
  }
}

Time-based gate:
stage('Production Deploy') {
  when {
    allOf {
      branch 'main'
      expression {
        def hour = new Date().hours
        return hour >= 9 && hour < 17 // 9 AM - 5 PM only
      }
    }
  }
}

Spinnaker supports advanced gates: canary analysis, external API checks, dependent pipeline completion.

Track deployment frequency, lead time, MTTR, change failure rate (DORA metrics). Implementation: 1) Pipeline metrics - build duration, test pass rate, deployment success rate, 2) Application metrics - post-deployment health, 3) Business metrics - user impact. Example instrumentation:
stage('Record Deployment') {
  steps {
    script {
      def deploymentStart = System.currentTimeMillis()
      // ... deployment steps
      def deploymentDuration = System.currentTimeMillis() - deploymentStart

      // Send to monitoring
      sh """
        curl -X POST datadog-api/metrics \
          -d '{"metric":"deployment.duration", "value":${deploymentDuration}, "tags":["service:payment","env:prod"]}'
      """

      // Track in database
      sh """
        psql -c "INSERT INTO deployments (service, version, environment, duration, status) 
                 VALUES ('payment', '${VERSION}', 'prod', ${deploymentDuration}, 'success')"
      """
    }
  }
}

Post-deployment verification:
stage('Post-Deploy Metrics') {
  steps {
    script {
      sleep(300) // 5 min warmup
      def metrics = sh(returnStdout: true, script: '''
        curl datadog-api/query?query=avg:trace.payment.latency{env:prod}
      ''').trim()

      def errorRate = sh(returnStdout: true, script: '''
        curl datadog-api/query?query=sum:trace.payment.errors{env:prod}/sum:trace.payment.requests{env:prod}
      ''').trim().toFloat()

      if (errorRate > 0.01) { // >1% errors
        sh 'kubectl rollout undo deployment/payment -n prod'
        error("High error rate: ${errorRate}, rolled back")
      }
    }
  }
}

Dashboards show: deployment frequency (DORA), lead time (commit to deploy), failure rate, rollback frequency. Continuous feedback loop for process improvement.

Regulated environments require audit trails, approvals, validation. Requirements: 1) Segregation of duties - different people code/review/deploy, 2) Audit trail - who deployed what when, 3) Compliance checks - security scans, vulnerability checks, 4) Rollback capability, 5) Environment parity validation, 6) Change management integration. Example pipeline:
stage('Compliance Checks') {
  steps {
    // Dependency vulnerability scan
    sh 'mvn org.owasp:dependency-check-maven:check'

    // SAST scan
    sh 'fortify scan'

    // License compliance
    sh 'license-maven-plugin:check'

    // HIPAA/SOC2 policy checks
    sh 'inspec exec hipaa-baseline'

    script {
      def criticalVulns = readJSON(file: 'vulnerability-report.json').critical
      if (criticalVulns > 0) {
        error("Critical vulnerabilities found, deployment blocked")
      }
    }
  }
}

stage('Change Management') {
  steps {
    script {
      // Create ServiceNow change request
      def changeRequest = sh(returnStdout: true, script: '''
        curl -X POST servicenow-api/change_request \
          -d '{"service":"payment", "version":"'${VERSION}'", "env":"prod"}'
      ''').trim()

      env.CHANGE_REQUEST_ID = changeRequest
    }
  }
}

stage('Security Team Approval') {
  steps {
    input(
      message: 'Security review required',
      submitter: 'security-team',
      parameters: [
        string(name: 'APPROVER_EMAIL', description: 'Your email'),
        text(name: 'REVIEW_NOTES', description: 'Security review notes')
      ]
    )
  }
}

stage('Deploy with Audit') {
  steps {
    script {
      // Log deployment
      sh """
        psql compliance_db -c "INSERT INTO deployments \
          (change_request, service, version, deployed_by, approved_by, timestamp) \
          VALUES ('${CHANGE_REQUEST_ID}', 'payment', '${VERSION}', '${BUILD_USER}', '${APPROVER_EMAIL}', NOW())"
      """

      // Deploy
      sh 'kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml'

      // Verify deployment matches approved artifact
      def runningImageHash = sh(returnStdout: true, script: 'kubectl get pod -l app=payment -o jsonpath="{.items[0].status.containerStatuses[0].imageID}"').trim()
      def approvedImageHash = env.APPROVED_IMAGE_HASH
      if (runningImageHash != approvedImageHash) {
        error("Deployed image doesn't match approved image")
      }
    }
  }
}

stage('Post-Deploy Validation') {
  steps {
    // Automated compliance tests
    sh './run-compliance-tests.sh prod'

    // Security posture validation
    sh 'prowler -M json > security-posture.json'
  }
}

4-eyes principle: developer != reviewer != deployer. Complete audit trail stored minimum 7 years. Rollback plan documented and tested quarterly.

Smoke tests verify basic functionality after deployment before declaring success. Should be: fast (<5 min), focused on critical paths, reliable (no flaky tests). Validate: 1) Application started (health endpoint), 2) Database connectivity, 3) External service integration, 4) Critical business workflows, 5) No errors in logs. Example smoke test suite:
@SpringBootTest(webEnvironment = WebEnvironment.DEFINED_PORT)
public class SmokeTests {

  private String baseUrl = System.getenv("APP_URL"); // https://staging.payment-service.com

  @Test
  public void healthCheckReturnsUp() {
    ResponseEntity<String> response = 
      restTemplate.getForEntity(baseUrl + "/actuator/health", String.class);
    assertThat(response.getStatusCode()).isEqualTo(HttpStatus.OK);
    assertThat(response.getBody()).contains("\"status\":\"UP\"");
  }

  @Test
  public void databaseConnectivity() {
    ResponseEntity<String> response = 
      restTemplate.getForEntity(baseUrl + "/actuator/health/db", String.class);
    assertThat(response.getBody()).contains("\"status\":\"UP\"");
  }

  @Test
  public void canProcessPayment() {
    PaymentRequest request = new PaymentRequest("test-order", 100.00);
    ResponseEntity<PaymentResponse> response = 
      restTemplate.postForEntity(baseUrl + "/api/payments", request, PaymentResponse.class);
    assertThat(response.getStatusCode()).isEqualTo(HttpStatus.OK);
    assertThat(response.getBody().getStatus()).isEqualTo("SUCCESS");
  }

  @Test
  public void noRecentErrorsInLogs() {
    // Query log aggregation
    String query = "service:payment level:error timestamp:[now-5m TO now]";
    List<LogEntry> errors = logClient.query(query);
    assertThat(errors).isEmpty();
  }
}

Pipeline integration:
stage('Smoke Tests') {
  steps {
    sh '''
      export APP_URL=https://staging.payment-service.com
      mvn test -Dtest=SmokeTests
    '''
