}

Smoke tests run immediately after deployment. Failure triggers automatic rollback. Different from integration tests (more comprehensive, slower). Critical for production confidence.

Deployment slots are separate instances of application (Azure App Service, AWS Elastic Beanstalk). Production slot serves live traffic, staging slot for pre-production validation. After validation, swap slots (instant cutover). Benefits: zero-downtime, full production-like testing, instant rollback (swap back), warm instances (no cold start). Azure App Service example:
# Deploy to staging slot
az webapp deployment source config-zip \
  --resource-group myRG \
  --name payment-app \
  --slot staging \
  --src payment-app.zip

# Test staging slot
curl https://payment-app-staging.azurewebsites.net/actuator/health

# Swap to production
az webapp deployment slot swap \
  --resource-group myRG \
  --name payment-app \
  --slot staging \
  --target-slot production

Swap is instant (routing change), no downtime. Rollback:
az webapp deployment slot swap --target-slot staging  # swap back

Pipeline integration:
stage('Deploy to Staging Slot') {
  steps {
    sh 'az webapp deploy --slot staging --src-path target/app.jar'
  }
}

stage('Validate Staging Slot') {
  steps {
    sh './run-tests.sh https://app-staging.azurewebsites.net'
  }
}

stage('Swap to Production') {
  steps {
    sh 'az webapp deployment slot swap --slot staging --target-slot production'
  }
}

stage('Verify Production') {
  steps {
    sh 'curl https://app.azurewebsites.net/health'
  }
}

Elastic Beanstalk similar concept: blue-green deployments with environment swapping. Staging slot testing includes: full integration tests, performance tests, security scans. After swap, monitor prod metrics for 15-30 min before considering deployment complete.

