Deployment metrics dashboard tracks DORA metrics and deployment health for engineering leaders and stakeholders. Key metrics: 1) Deployment frequency, 2) Lead time for changes, 3) Change failure rate, 4) Mean time to recovery, 5) Deployment success rate, 6) Deployment duration. Implementation:

**Data Collection**
Pipeline instrumentation:
post {
  always {
    script {
      def deploymentData = [
        service: env.APP_NAME,
        version: env.BUILD_VERSION,
        environment: env.DEPLOY_ENV,
        status: currentBuild.result,
        startTime: currentBuild.startTimeInMillis,
        duration: currentBuild.duration,
        triggeredBy: currentBuild.getBuildCauses()[0].userId,
        gitCommit: env.GIT_COMMIT,
        gitBranch: env.GIT_BRANCH,
        testsPassed: env.TESTS_PASSED,
        testsFailed: env.TESTS_FAILED
      ]

      // Store in database
      sh """
        curl -X POST metrics-api/deployments \
          -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
          -d '${JsonOutput.toJson(deploymentData)}'
      """

      // Send to time-series database
      sh """
        echo "deployment,service=${env.APP_NAME},env=${env.DEPLOY_ENV},status=${currentBuild.result} duration=${currentBuild.duration},count=1" | \
          curl -XPOST 'http://influxdb:8086/write?db=cicd' --data-binary @-
      """
    }
  }
}

